1
00:00:09,142 --> 00:00:13,234
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:14,882 --> 00:00:17,093
You know, maybe I SHOULD keep moving,

3
00:00:17,093 --> 00:00:21,223
because they probably WILL teleport
behind me, then collapse the building.

4
00:00:21,223 --> 00:00:25,500
Then, they win because they're
aliens, so who cares, and I'm dead.

5
00:00:26,598 --> 00:00:28,827
So, is this the reactor room or what?

6
00:00:28,827 --> 00:00:30,939
It looks pretty flooded to me.

7
00:00:30,939 --> 00:00:33,427
Jeez, that's a lot of blood on the wall.

8
00:00:33,427 --> 00:00:37,500
I don't think the aliens did that.
The splatter velocity's too high.

9
00:00:38,978 --> 00:00:41,720
Oh, there's an entrance there.

10
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:43,796
Shit, that's kind of deep.

11
00:00:43,796 --> 00:00:46,802
I guess this suit lets me sink
down pretty fast.

12
00:00:46,802 --> 00:00:48,188
I don't know.

13
00:00:48,188 --> 00:00:51,200
The stakes are pretty high,
but--Oh, my God!

14
00:00:52,257 --> 00:00:55,061
How did I not see this? Am I blind?!

15
00:00:55,061 --> 00:00:57,033
This kit might have morphine!

16
00:00:58,110 --> 00:01:01,091
Yes, here it is! Morphine sulfate!

17
00:01:01,091 --> 00:01:02,704
Aahhh...

18
00:01:02,704 --> 00:01:04,612
Yeah, I'll start feeling this soon.

19
00:01:04,612 --> 00:01:07,152
Oh, my God, did I need this!

20
00:01:07,152 --> 00:01:09,218
This is fucking perfect.

21
00:01:09,218 --> 00:01:12,118
Alright, let's get the blood
flowing so this kicks in!

22
00:01:12,118 --> 00:01:14,425
A cold swim should do just the trick.

23
00:01:14,425 --> 00:01:16,000
Time to go save the world!

24
00:01:18,431 --> 00:01:29,123
[underwater mumbling]

25
00:01:29,123 --> 00:01:32,959
[gasping]

26
00:01:32,959 --> 00:01:35,001
I don't think I'm feeling it, yet.

27
00:01:35,001 --> 00:01:36,820
Maybe... I don't know.

28
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:37,898
"Radiation".

29
00:01:37,898 --> 00:01:41,868
Well, I'm either getting a
little bit or a lifetime supply.

30
00:01:42,996 --> 00:01:44,033
[inhale]

31
00:01:47,995 --> 00:01:49,601
[underwater mumbling]

32
00:01:51,269 --> 00:01:53,141
Well, this COULD be the reactor.

33
00:01:53,141 --> 00:01:56,434
Honestly, we own so much huge
machinery, I have no idea.

34
00:01:57,924 --> 00:01:58,969
[underwater straining]

35
00:01:58,969 --> 00:02:03,500
[underwater panicking]

36
00:02:04,789 --> 00:02:07,276
Okay, that's partially flooded.

37
00:02:07,276 --> 00:02:11,667
Soon, I'll get back to long-term panic
instead of all this short-term panic.

38
00:02:14,273 --> 00:02:15,133
[underwater straining]

39
00:02:21,719 --> 00:02:23,865
It's flooded! I'm a hero!

40
00:02:23,865 --> 00:02:24,801
[vortigaunt charging up]
What the hell?

41
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:27,688
Man, fuck you!

42
00:02:28,742 --> 00:02:32,407
I just saved your life from a
meltdown, I'm a hero!

43
00:02:32,407 --> 00:02:35,033
You can't zap me like that, I'm a hero!

44
00:02:35,591 --> 00:02:36,567
Yeah!

45
00:02:38,342 --> 00:02:39,544
Jesus.

46
00:02:39,544 --> 00:02:42,613
Electricity does not respect my heroism.

47
00:02:43,324 --> 00:02:46,133
Well, I guess climbing out of
here is a good idea, right?

48
00:02:46,809 --> 00:02:47,572
Right.

49
00:02:47,572 --> 00:02:48,436
I don't get it.

50
00:02:48,436 --> 00:02:52,734
Why is there so much arcing-BLAAAAH!
AAAH! AAAH-AAAAH-AAAAAH!

51
00:02:53,542 --> 00:02:57,148
Huh, maybe being on a metal
ladder isn't so smart, either,

52
00:02:57,148 --> 00:02:59,303
especially since I'm still wet?

53
00:02:59,303 --> 00:03:00,264
Uhh...

54
00:03:00,264 --> 00:03:01,600
Okay, I didn't feel much.

55
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:05,374
I guess my boots have some insulation
in them. Or maybe it's the morphine.

56
00:03:05,374 --> 00:03:06,328
Hmmm.

57
00:03:06,328 --> 00:03:08,250
Alright, time to go jump the--

58
00:03:08,250 --> 00:03:12,074
[shuddering, screaming]

59
00:03:12,074 --> 00:03:13,895
Shit, I think I made a mistake.

60
00:03:13,895 --> 00:03:18,240
I don't think I flooded the reactor;
I THINK THIS IS THE GENERATOR, GOD DAMMIT!

61
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:19,538
WHY WOULD THEY FLOOD THAT?!

62
00:03:19,538 --> 00:03:22,103
THAT WOULD JUST BE
DANGEROUS AND BREAK THINGS!

63
00:03:22,103 --> 00:03:23,490
GRRAAAAAAAAAAGH!

64
00:03:23,490 --> 00:03:26,162
GOTTA GET OUT OF TORTURE CHAMBER!

65
00:03:26,162 --> 00:03:28,759
I DON'T NEED ELECTROSHOCK THERAPY!

66
00:03:28,759 --> 00:03:30,567
I ALREADY HAVE MY--YAAAAAH!

67
00:03:30,968 --> 00:03:32,400
Fucking shit!

68
00:03:37,415 --> 00:03:40,308
I'm getting out of here before
it melts through the door.

69
00:03:40,308 --> 00:03:42,761
I'm feeling pretty good, though.

70
00:03:42,761 --> 00:03:47,248
I haven't felt this good since...
yesterday when I got to the surface

71
00:03:47,248 --> 00:03:48,956
and thought I was going to leave.

72
00:03:48,956 --> 00:03:53,736
Except then the military started
bombing the place, then I felt... bad.

73
00:03:53,736 --> 00:03:56,762
Hey, "Supplies", I like supplies.

74
00:03:56,762 --> 00:03:58,312
[Geiger counter ticking]
Okay, not the radioactivity.

75
00:03:58,312 --> 00:04:01,317
I have enough of that. Thank you. No.

76
00:04:01,317 --> 00:04:04,167
Hey, this looks civilized.
Where does this go?

77
00:04:04,569 --> 00:04:05,033
Up.

78
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:07,801
Okay, where's the button?

79
00:04:08,469 --> 00:04:11,321
Oh, there is no button. It must
be on the outside.

80
00:04:11,321 --> 00:04:12,166
[button buzzes]

81
00:04:12,166 --> 00:04:14,734
We design a lot of elevators like that.

82
00:04:14,734 --> 00:04:17,407
Oh, I see. The button doesn't work.

83
00:04:17,407 --> 00:04:19,503
We design a lot like that, too.

84
00:04:19,503 --> 00:04:20,901
Okay, I can climb.

85
00:04:22,328 --> 00:04:24,835
An old-fashioned elevator.

86
00:04:24,835 --> 00:04:27,254
The kind that's powered by... ladders.

87
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:30,262
[metal groaning]

88
00:04:30,262 --> 00:04:31,367
What was that?

89
00:04:33,790 --> 00:04:34,734
Well, where's the...?

90
00:04:36,239 --> 00:04:39,631
Oh, come on, guys.
You can design this better.

91
00:04:39,631 --> 00:04:41,726
All right, I'm...

92
00:04:41,726 --> 00:04:42,434
Batman.

93
00:04:43,842 --> 00:04:45,662
Yeah-ha-ha-ha!

94
00:04:45,662 --> 00:04:47,288
Yeah, this is great.

95
00:04:47,288 --> 00:04:48,631
"SUPPLIES"!

96
00:04:48,631 --> 00:04:50,329
I like supplies.

97
00:04:50,329 --> 00:04:52,567
Let's get some supplies.

98
00:04:52,567 --> 00:04:55,192
Oh, wow, more drugs.

99
00:04:55,192 --> 00:04:59,085
I-I don't know. I'm feeling
pretty good now.

100
00:04:59,085 --> 00:05:00,408
Okay, I'll take this.

101
00:05:00,408 --> 00:05:02,005
That's... yeah.

102
00:05:02,005 --> 00:05:04,406
I don't know. I might overdose.

103
00:05:04,406 --> 00:05:06,400
What do you think, Mr. Crate?

104
00:05:07,713 --> 00:05:10,146
Yeah, you always know what to say.

105
00:05:10,146 --> 00:05:12,267
I'd better play it safe.

106
00:05:13,110 --> 00:05:15,234
Oh, wow. What the fuck are you?

107
00:05:15,931 --> 00:05:16,217
GUARD: Sir?

108
00:05:16,217 --> 00:05:17,267
You're blue.

109
00:05:18,095 --> 00:05:20,278
That's a tragedy, really.

110
00:05:20,278 --> 00:05:22,167
You look like all the others.

111
00:05:23,099 --> 00:05:25,334
I should go and fix that for you.

112
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,920
GUARD: I'd like to get my hands--
Stop mumbling.

113
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:29,055
GUARD: Hey, Gordon.

114
00:05:29,055 --> 00:05:32,150
Oh, wow. You know my name.
That's amazing.

115
00:05:32,150 --> 00:05:34,772
Well, you SHOULD! I'm a hero!

116
00:05:34,772 --> 00:05:35,381
Ooooh!

117
00:05:35,381 --> 00:05:37,959
GUARD: Yep, all that target
range time is gonna pay off today.

118
00:05:37,959 --> 00:05:40,585
You're right. Why fight temptation?

119
00:05:40,585 --> 00:05:41,889
[health charger beeps]

120
00:05:41,889 --> 00:05:44,113
[health charger beeps]
Yeah, I can handle some more...

121
00:05:44,113 --> 00:05:45,849
[health charger beeps]
I'm a hero!

122
00:05:45,849 --> 00:05:48,384
HEV: Morphine administered.

123
00:05:48,384 --> 00:05:50,427
Fuck, yeah!

124
00:05:50,427 --> 00:05:53,914
I am ready to face everything!

125
00:05:53,914 --> 00:05:56,895
I'm feeling a little drowsy,
but that's cool.

126
00:05:56,895 --> 00:05:58,179
I'm very chill.

127
00:05:58,179 --> 00:05:59,334
What's this?

128
00:06:01,035 --> 00:06:02,353
Okay...

129
00:06:02,353 --> 00:06:07,956
I think I just watched some guy kill
himself by walking into the portable sun.

130
00:06:07,956 --> 00:06:10,268
I didn't know we had one of those.

131
00:06:10,268 --> 00:06:12,498
Or that they even existed.

132
00:06:12,498 --> 00:06:14,512
Whoooaaaaaah...

133
00:06:14,512 --> 00:06:15,634
Wake up time!

134
00:06:19,284 --> 00:06:22,270
Hah! I didn't even feel that!

135
00:06:22,270 --> 00:06:23,676
Hey, how are you doing?

136
00:06:23,676 --> 00:06:25,541
I feel great!

137
00:06:25,541 --> 00:06:27,286
Hey, I've gotta ask you something...

138
00:06:27,286 --> 00:06:29,484
What do you know about nuclear fusion?

139
00:06:29,484 --> 00:06:31,754
Nothing, right? Yeah, I didn't think so.

140
00:06:31,754 --> 00:06:31,982
Oh!

141
00:06:32,820 --> 00:06:33,834
Now, YOU...!

142
00:06:35,422 --> 00:06:38,084
I know YOU don't know anything.

143
00:06:38,084 --> 00:06:42,269
Hey, listen, these monsters are
interrupting my train of thought.

144
00:06:42,269 --> 00:06:46,161
So, you need to talk to the administrator
and tell him to stop it, all right?

145
00:06:46,161 --> 00:06:47,354
Just stop it.

146
00:06:47,354 --> 00:06:51,093
We've got enough monsters for
at least nine weeks.

147
00:06:51,093 --> 00:06:53,076
This is total overkill.

148
00:06:53,076 --> 00:06:55,843
[straining]
I was meant to turn this...

149
00:06:55,843 --> 00:06:58,351
That did... something.

150
00:06:58,351 --> 00:07:01,835
"Radiation Hazard"--they're bluffing...

151
00:07:01,835 --> 00:07:03,037
Raaaah...

152
00:07:03,037 --> 00:07:05,556
I wanted to see the portable sun.

153
00:07:05,556 --> 00:07:08,899
How did we do that?
That's fusion power!

154
00:07:08,899 --> 00:07:12,334
And we have it here all
tucked--Whoooooah...

155
00:07:12,951 --> 00:07:16,654
Oh, shit... no. I don't
think I trust this, yet.

156
00:07:16,654 --> 00:07:18,435
It glows.

157
00:07:18,435 --> 00:07:19,361
Buttons!

158
00:07:19,361 --> 00:07:22,214
[tapping buttons]

159
00:07:22,214 --> 00:07:23,261
No...

160
00:07:23,261 --> 00:07:25,953
Jesus Christ! What am I looking at?

161
00:07:25,953 --> 00:07:27,435
Is this a star?

162
00:07:27,435 --> 00:07:30,548
Did we create a fucking
star in a box somehow?

163
00:07:30,548 --> 00:07:32,305
I didn't feel any heat off it.

164
00:07:32,305 --> 00:07:34,494
Did we figure out cold fusion?

165
00:07:34,494 --> 00:07:39,424
Cold fusion has been the butt of physics
jokes forever; it's an embarrassment.

166
00:07:39,424 --> 00:07:42,731
Isn't that in the Journal of
Irreproducible Results?

167
00:07:42,731 --> 00:07:43,684
But, you know what?

168
00:07:43,684 --> 00:07:48,930
I bet those guys didn't have spinning
energy balls just hovering and...

169
00:07:48,930 --> 00:07:50,899
trying to read my mind.

170
00:07:50,899 --> 00:07:53,357
Why am I seeing more of these down here?

171
00:07:53,357 --> 00:07:56,151
This is obviously just a storage area.

172
00:07:56,151 --> 00:07:58,660
Maybe I took too much morphine...

173
00:07:58,660 --> 00:08:01,734
But, fuck that! I can walk and everything.

174
00:08:01,734 --> 00:08:04,701
And I feel so good!

175
00:08:06,495 --> 00:08:07,659
Buttons!

176
00:08:07,659 --> 00:08:09,587
Zooba-dabba-dooba-dabba-dabba-da!

177
00:08:09,587 --> 00:08:12,512
It's cold fusion; how come I'm
not in this department?

178
00:08:12,512 --> 00:08:14,000
There must be an explanation.

179
00:08:16,935 --> 00:08:19,057
This is my explanation?!

180
00:08:19,057 --> 00:08:20,603
I don't understand!

181
00:08:20,603 --> 00:08:22,290
This is too interpretive.

182
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:25,032
I don't have to take this, I'm a hero!

183
00:08:25,032 --> 00:08:26,912
Hey, are you an oracle?

184
00:08:26,912 --> 00:08:29,677
No, you don't look like one.

185
00:08:29,677 --> 00:08:32,133
Hey, this is just like Dirty Harry.

186
00:08:33,209 --> 00:08:34,643
A long-range scene.

187
00:08:34,643 --> 00:08:36,954
No, wait. It was one of the sequels.

188
00:08:36,954 --> 00:08:38,968
That's my favorite Dirty Harry movie.

189
00:08:40,095 --> 00:08:43,861
The one where he guns down the
giant monster with the tentacle arms.

190
00:08:46,606 --> 00:08:49,700
"Make my day, squidface."

191
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:52,490
Ehh, you're not as big
as the one in the movie.

192
00:08:52,490 --> 00:08:55,034
I feel like skipping through the hallway.

193
00:08:55,034 --> 00:08:56,335
It's a nice big one.

194
00:08:56,335 --> 00:08:58,547
Oh, what's in here? Awww.

195
00:08:58,547 --> 00:09:02,377
Maybe I won't skip. It's kind of
heavy with the suit and the guns...

196
00:09:02,377 --> 00:09:03,373
...and the bang...

197
00:09:03,373 --> 00:09:04,852
...and more bang...

198
00:09:04,852 --> 00:09:06,292
...bang-bang...

199
00:09:06,292 --> 00:09:07,267
...and kaboom...

200
00:09:07,267 --> 00:09:08,667
...and... oh boy...

201
00:09:11,419 --> 00:09:12,817
Blaaaaghaaghgagh!

202
00:09:12,817 --> 00:09:14,021
Bugs...

203
00:09:14,021 --> 00:09:16,577
Man, you guys made
this hallway all dirty.

204
00:09:16,577 --> 00:09:17,667
Why did you do that?

205
00:09:18,192 --> 00:09:21,735
It was nice and squeaky clean
before you showed up.

206
00:09:21,735 --> 00:09:23,746
It made me want to roll around in it.

207
00:09:23,746 --> 00:09:25,546
I don't want to do that anymore.

208
00:09:25,546 --> 00:09:27,140
Well, this is a little better.

209
00:09:27,140 --> 00:09:28,439
Where my lab at?

210
00:09:28,439 --> 00:09:29,823
[door buzzes]
Bahh!

211
00:09:29,823 --> 00:09:34,546
Ah, okay, I think I figured out
what this place is.

212
00:09:34,546 --> 00:09:38,801
This is where we take all the
VIPs looking to fund the place.

213
00:09:38,801 --> 00:09:42,036
There are labs but they're all a
little too clean.

214
00:09:42,036 --> 00:09:44,016
Oh, shit, not this one.

215
00:09:44,016 --> 00:09:45,363
What the hell happened here?

216
00:09:45,363 --> 00:09:48,651
That splatter mark looks like
this guy fell two stories.

217
00:09:48,651 --> 00:09:50,657
How does somebody trip like that?

218
00:09:50,657 --> 00:09:52,287
[Geiger counter ticking]
And we're leaking radiation;

219
00:09:52,287 --> 00:09:53,989
[Geiger counter ticking]
this is not part of the tour.

220
00:09:53,989 --> 00:09:57,435
But, yeah, we take the VIPs
here, show them the energy balls,

221
00:09:57,435 --> 00:10:00,576
they don't know anything so they're
impressed and give us more money,

222
00:10:00,576 --> 00:10:03,836
when the reality is they're
holograms. I'm sure of it.

223
00:10:03,836 --> 00:10:07,774
Yeah, see, look at that pad
underneath; these are holograms!

224
00:10:07,774 --> 00:10:09,810
Wow. A lot of them.

225
00:10:09,810 --> 00:10:12,585
Those rotating platforms are cool, too.

226
00:10:12,585 --> 00:10:16,391
Yeah, this would impress the hell out
of me if I didn't know anything.

227
00:10:16,391 --> 00:10:21,662
In fact, it STILL impresses me,
because I'm kind of high?

228
00:10:21,662 --> 00:10:23,199
Yee-hahahaha...

229
00:10:23,199 --> 00:10:25,540
Oh, wow, this looks dangerous.

230
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:28,703
Yeah, there's a certain percentage
of the public that believes,

231
00:10:28,703 --> 00:10:33,388
unless you have robots or glowing
lights, that science isn't happening.

232
00:10:33,388 --> 00:10:37,305
But, we have BOTH. That's why
we're so well-funded.

233
00:10:37,305 --> 00:10:40,640
Some people expect chemistry
sets and dry ice fog,

234
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:43,285
but I think we have some
rooms for that, too.

235
00:10:43,285 --> 00:10:48,366
Okay, I'm going to test my theory
like a TRUE scientist on drugs.

236
00:10:48,366 --> 00:10:49,100
Da-DAH!

237
00:10:49,911 --> 00:10:52,613
I didn't feel anything. At all.

238
00:10:52,613 --> 00:10:54,000
Okay, I'm going to walk...

239
00:10:54,715 --> 00:10:56,926
Yeah, it's totally a hologram!

240
00:10:56,926 --> 00:10:58,402
Heeehhhh...

241
00:10:58,402 --> 00:11:03,139
Well, I could stare at these a long
time, the way I'm feeling right now

242
00:11:03,139 --> 00:11:04,481
but I still don't know where

243
00:11:04,481 --> 00:11:04,934
[bzzt]

